WEBVTT

00:00:09,070 --> 00:00:17,070
Can any of the toxicity labs, if we want to retest, be covered by insurance?

00:00:17,070 --> 00:00:18,070
No.

00:00:18,070 --> 00:00:29,070
So, none of the like the mosaic or toxicity labs or parasite labs or any of the functional medicine labs are never going to be covered by insurance.

00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:32,070
So, but I have really good insurance.

00:00:32,070 --> 00:00:34,070
I have Medicare plus blah blah blah.

00:00:34,070 --> 00:00:35,070
It's still not going to be covered.

00:00:35,070 --> 00:00:36,070
It's not going to be covered.

00:00:37,070 --> 00:00:45,070
Now, if you have like Samaritan's ministries, which technically isn't a insurance, we've had people get that cover.

00:00:45,070 --> 00:00:51,070
It covered under that, but that's pretty much the only one.

00:00:51,070 --> 00:00:57,070
So, and that is you still have to pay for it and then you submit it and hope they cover it.

00:00:57,070 --> 00:01:06,070
So, that's not a for sure thing, but insurance is not going to cover any of the other functional labs.

00:01:06,070 --> 00:01:15,070
Now, insurance may cover a CBC with the forageal and a couple heads of metabolic panel and a tumor marker panel.

00:01:15,070 --> 00:01:19,070
If it's ordered by your primary practitioner.

00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:26,070
But many times you go into the primary practitioner and you say, this is what I want.

00:01:26,070 --> 00:01:30,070
And they order something completely different.

00:01:30,070 --> 00:01:32,070
But it's worth a shot.

00:01:32,070 --> 00:01:38,070
I mean, if you can get your Medicare to cover some of those labs, and that's just money in your pocket.

00:01:38,070 --> 00:01:40,070
You paid for it in the first place.

00:01:40,070 --> 00:01:43,070
I think you should try to do that.

00:01:43,070 --> 00:01:50,070
It also presupposes that you have a medical doctor that you have a relationship with.

00:01:50,070 --> 00:01:58,070
So, I always try to get people, encourage people to seek that out if they can so that they can get.

00:01:58,070 --> 00:02:01,070
So, we can get regular labs.

00:02:01,070 --> 00:02:06,070
It would be the functional medicine labs, but regular labs covered and done on a regular basis.

00:02:06,070 --> 00:02:17,070
I just think the more frequently that we could do those labs, the more objective data that we have to formulate a working...

00:02:17,070 --> 00:02:27,070
and diagnose the criteria of how to move forward and where you're at and how we're progressing.

00:02:27,070 --> 00:02:31,070
So, the more data we have, the better.

